---
layout: layouts/staff.njk
staffPage: ministry
staffNum: "04"
staffTitle: Ministry
staffHeading: What this ministry <b>publishes</b>
staffHint: four sections, all of them visible to anyone once published
---
{#- FOUR SECTIONS, ONE PAGE.

   Milestones, giving goals, prayer and videos are the same job — the things a
   ministry says about itself in public — and each is small. Four nav entries
   for four short pages crowded the bar and made them look unrelated.

   Every section is built the same way, deliberately: a view switch at the top,
   an EDIT half that is a list of rows opening into a form, and an AS EMBEDDED
   half that is the real widget plus the code to paste. Learning one teaches
   all three. -#}

<div class="tabs" role="tablist">
  <button type="button" class="tab" role="tab" data-tab="milestones"
          aria-selected="true" data-i18n="min.milestones">Milestones</button>
  <button type="button" class="tab" role="tab" data-tab="goals"
          aria-selected="false" data-i18n="min.goals">Goals</button>
  <button type="button" class="tab" role="tab" data-tab="prayer"
          aria-selected="false" data-i18n="min.prayer">Prayer</button>
  <button type="button" class="tab" role="tab" data-tab="videos"
          aria-selected="false" data-i18n="min.videos">Videos</button>
</div>

<!-- ========================================================== MILESTONES -->
<section class="tab-panel" data-panel="milestones" role="tabpanel">
  {% set embedWidget = "roadmap" %}
  {% include "embed-panel.njk" %}

  <div data-emb-content>
<div class="ms-bar">
  <button type="button" class="solid-btn" id="msAdd" data-i18n="ms.add">Add milestone</button>
  <span class="hint" id="msStatus"></span>
</div>


{#- Said plainly and near the toggles, because this is the one screen in the
   console where a mistake is visible to strangers rather than to staff. -#}
<p class="note ms-note" data-i18n-html="ms.publishedLeave"><b>Published entries leave this building.</b> Anything switched to Published is
  served to partner websites through the public API and can be read by anyone.
  New milestones start unpublished.</p>

<div class="ms-list" id="msList">
  <p class="empty" data-i18n="common.loading">Loading…</p>
</div>

{#- Where the editor panel lives when it is not attached under a row.

   It has to live OUTSIDE #msList: render() rebuilds that list with innerHTML,
   which destroyed the form element whenever the list refreshed while the panel
   was open — after which Edit could never reopen it, because the element it
   looked for no longer existed. -#}
<div id="msFormHolder"></div>

{#- One form, reused for create and edit. Hidden until opened. -#}
<form class="ms-form" id="msForm" hidden>
  <input type="hidden" id="msId">

  {#- TWO LANGUAGE COLUMNS, EITHER OF WHICH CAN BE ANY LANGUAGE.

     Not "English and Croatian": the columns are built from whatever the
     organisation offers, so adding Portuguese needs no change here. The left
     column opens on the staff member's own language and the right on the next
     one they publish, but both are free to change.

     Side by side because a missing or stale translation is invisible when you
     edit one language at a time — which is how a trilingual site ends up with
     three versions that disagree. -#}
  <div class="ms-langs">
    <div class="ms-col">
      <div class="ms-col-head">
        <select id="msLangA" class="lang-pick" aria-label="Language, left column"></select>
        <span class="ms-col-tag" id="msTagA"></span>
      </div>
      <label class="fld"><span data-i18n="ms.title">Title</span>
        <input type="text" data-tx="title" data-col="a" maxlength="200"></label>
      <label class="fld"><span data-i18n="ms.description">Description</span>
        <textarea data-tx="description" data-col="a" rows="5"></textarea></label>
      <label class="fld"><span data-i18n="ms.when">When</span> <em data-i18n="ms.freeText">free text</em>
        <input type="text" data-tx="target_label" data-col="a" maxlength="120"
               placeholder="End of September 2027"></label>
    </div>

    <div class="ms-col">
      <div class="ms-col-head">
        <select id="msLangB" class="lang-pick" aria-label="Language, right column"></select>
        <span class="ms-col-tag" id="msTagB"></span>
      </div>
      <label class="fld"><span data-i18n="ms.title">Title</span>
        <input type="text" data-tx="title" data-col="b" maxlength="200"></label>
      <label class="fld"><span data-i18n="ms.description">Description</span>
        <textarea data-tx="description" data-col="b" rows="5"></textarea></label>
      <label class="fld"><span data-i18n="ms.when">When</span> <em data-i18n="ms.freeText">free text</em>
        <input type="text" data-tx="target_label" data-col="b" maxlength="120"></label>
    </div>
  </div>

  {#- Language-neutral: true regardless of which language you are reading. -#}
  <div class="ms-grid ms-neutral">
    <label class="fld">
      <span data-i18n="ms.sortDate">Sort date</span> <em data-i18n="ms.orderingOnly">for ordering only</em>
      <input type="date" id="msDate">
    </label>
    <label class="fld">
      <span data-i18n="ms.status">Status</span>
      <select id="msStatusSel">
        <option value="upcoming" data-i18n="ms.upcoming">Upcoming</option>
        <option value="in_progress" data-i18n="ms.inProgress">In progress</option>
        <option value="complete" data-i18n="ms.complete">Complete</option>
        <option value="cancelled" data-i18n="ms.cancelled">Cancelled</option>
      </select>
    </label>
    <label class="fld">
      <span data-i18n="ms.completion">Completion</span> <em data-i18n="ms.percent">percent</em>
      <input type="number" id="msCompletion" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="0">
    </label>
    <label class="fld">
      <span data-i18n="ms.partOf">Part of</span> <em data-i18n="ms.optional">optional</em>
      <select id="msParent"><option value="" data-i18n="ms.topLevel">— top level —</option></select>
    </label>
  </div>

  <div class="ms-switches">
    <button type="button" class="switch" id="msPublic" role="switch" aria-checked="false">
      <span class="switch-track"><span class="switch-state">Off</span><span class="switch-knob"></span></span>
      <span class="switch-label"><span data-i18n="ms.published">Published</span>
        <span class="switch-note" data-i18n="ms.publishedNote">Visible on partner websites</span>
      </span>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="switch" id="msFeatured" role="switch" aria-checked="false">
      <span class="switch-track"><span class="switch-state">Off</span><span class="switch-knob"></span></span>
      <span class="switch-label"><span data-i18n="ms.featured">Featured</span>
        <span class="switch-note" data-i18n="ms.featuredNote">Highlighted on their home page</span>
      </span>
    </button>
  </div>

  <div class="ms-actions">
    <button type="submit" class="solid-btn" data-i18n="ms.apply">Apply</button>
    <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="msCancel" data-i18n="ms.cancel">Cancel</button>
    {#- "Apply" not "Save": this closes the form and updates the list, but
       nothing reaches the database until Save changes is pressed. Calling
       both of them Save is how people end up believing work is safe. -#}
    <span class="hint" id="msFormStatus" data-i18n="ms.applyNote">Applies to the list — save to publish</span>
  </div>
</form>

{#- Only appears when something is actually unsaved, so its presence is the
   signal. Fixed to the bottom of the viewport and LAST in the document, so
   reading order matches what you see — a bar announced before the content
   it refers to reads oddly to a screen reader.

   role=status so the change in count is announced without stealing focus
   from whatever is being edited. -#}
  </div>
</section>

<!-- =============================================================== GOALS -->
<section class="tab-panel" data-panel="goals" role="tabpanel" hidden>
  {% set embedWidget = "goal" %}
  {% include "embed-panel.njk" %}

  <div data-emb-content>
    <div class="ms-bar">
      <button type="button" class="solid-btn" id="glAdd" data-i18n="gl.add">Add goal</button>
      <span class="hint" id="glStatus"></span>
    </div>

    <p class="note ms-note" data-i18n-html="gl.publishedNote"><b>Published goals leave this building.</b> A goal switched to Published is
      served to partner websites and can be read by anyone. It carries no donor
      records — only the target, the amount raised and a count.</p>

    <div class="ms-list" id="glList">
      <p class="empty" data-i18n="common.loading">Loading…</p>
    </div>

    <div id="glFormHolder"></div>

    {#- One form for create and edit, like the milestone editor. Goals are NOT
       translated — `label` has always been a plain column — so there are no
       language columns here. Giving them a translations table is its own
       migration and its own editing surface. -#}
    <form class="ms-form" id="glForm" hidden>
      <input type="hidden" id="glId">

      <div class="ms-grid ms-neutral">
        <label class="fld gl-wide">
          <span data-i18n="gl.name">Name</span>
          <input type="text" id="glLabel" maxlength="120" placeholder="Monthly support">
        </label>
        <label class="fld gl-wide">
          <span data-i18n="gl.description">Description</span>
          <textarea id="glDescription" rows="3" maxlength="600"
                    placeholder="What this is for."></textarea>
        </label>
        <label class="fld">
          <span data-i18n="gl.kind">Kind</span>
          <select id="glKind">
            <option value="monthly" data-i18n="gl.monthly">Monthly</option>
            <option value="one_time" data-i18n="gl.oneTime">One time</option>
            <option value="project" data-i18n="gl.project">Project</option>
          </select>
        </label>
        <label class="fld">
          <span data-i18n="gl.target">Target</span>
          <input type="number" id="glTarget" min="1" step="1" placeholder="4500">
        </label>
        <label class="fld">
          <span data-i18n="gl.currency">Currency</span>
          <input type="text" id="glCurrency" maxlength="3" value="USD"
                 spellcheck="false" placeholder="USD">
        </label>
      </div>

      {#- PROGRESS IS A SEPARATE ACT. It is a reading taken at a moment, not a
         property of the goal, so it is appended as a snapshot and the newest
         one wins. That is why a mistyped figure is corrected by entering the
         right one rather than by editing the past — and why an importer
         hooked up tomorrow needs no migration. -#}
      <div class="gl-progress">
        <h4 data-i18n="gl.progressTitle">Where it stands</h4>
        <p data-i18n="gl.progressNote">Entered by hand until a giving platform is connected. Each entry is kept, and the most recent is the one shown.</p>
        <div class="ms-grid">
          <label class="fld">
            <span data-i18n="gl.raised">Raised</span>
            <input type="number" id="glRaised" min="0" step="1" placeholder="3060">
          </label>
          <label class="fld">
            <span data-i18n="gl.donors">Partners giving</span>
            <em data-i18n="ms.optional">optional</em>
            <input type="number" id="glDonors" min="0" step="1" placeholder="14">
          </label>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ms-switches">
        <button type="button" class="switch" id="glPublic" role="switch" aria-checked="false">
          <span class="switch-track"><span class="switch-state">Off</span><span class="switch-knob"></span></span>
          <span class="switch-label"><span data-i18n="ms.published">Published</span>
            <span class="switch-note" data-i18n="ms.publishedNote">Visible on partner websites</span>
          </span>
        </button>
      </div>

      <div class="ms-actions">
        <button type="submit" class="solid-btn" data-i18n="gl.save">Save goal</button>
        <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="glCancel" data-i18n="ms.cancel">Cancel</button>
        {#- Unlike milestones, a goal saves STRAIGHT AWAY. There is no working
           copy to reconcile: one goal is one row, and a save bar for a single
           small form is ceremony. -#}
        <span class="hint" id="glFormStatus" data-i18n="gl.savesNow">Saves immediately</span>
      </div>
    </form>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================== PRAYER -->
<section class="tab-panel" data-panel="prayer" role="tabpanel" hidden>
  {% set embedWidget = "prayer" %}
  {% include "embed-panel.njk" %}

  <div data-emb-content>
    <div class="ms-bar">
      <button type="button" class="solid-btn" id="prAdd" data-i18n="pr.add">Add request</button>
      <span class="hint" id="prStatus"></span>
    </div>

    <p class="note ms-note" data-i18n-html="pr.publishedNote"><b>Published requests leave this building.</b> Write them as you would want
      them read by a stranger — anything switched to Published is served to
      partner websites. New requests start unpublished.</p>

    <div class="ms-list" id="prList">
      <p class="empty" data-i18n="common.loading">Loading…</p>
    </div>

    <div id="prFormHolder"></div>

    <form class="ms-form" id="prForm" hidden>
      <input type="hidden" id="prId">

      {#- Two language columns, same as the milestone editor and for the same
         reason: a missing or stale translation is invisible when you edit one
         language at a time. -#}
      <div class="ms-langs">
        <div class="ms-col">
          <div class="ms-col-head">
            <select id="prLangA" class="lang-pick" aria-label="Language, left column"></select>
            <span class="ms-col-tag" id="prTagA"></span>
          </div>
          <label class="fld"><span data-i18n="pr.title">Request</span>
            <input type="text" data-ptx="title" data-col="a" maxlength="160"></label>
          <label class="fld"><span data-i18n="pr.detail">Detail</span>
            <textarea data-ptx="description" data-col="a" rows="4"></textarea></label>
          <label class="fld"><span data-i18n="pr.answerText">What happened</span>
            <em data-i18n="pr.whenAnswered">once answered</em>
            <textarea data-ptx="answer_text" data-col="a" rows="3"></textarea></label>
        </div>

        <div class="ms-col">
          <div class="ms-col-head">
            <select id="prLangB" class="lang-pick" aria-label="Language, right column"></select>
            <span class="ms-col-tag" id="prTagB"></span>
          </div>
          <label class="fld"><span data-i18n="pr.title">Request</span>
            <input type="text" data-ptx="title" data-col="b" maxlength="160"></label>
          <label class="fld"><span data-i18n="pr.detail">Detail</span>
            <textarea data-ptx="description" data-col="b" rows="4"></textarea></label>
          <label class="fld"><span data-i18n="pr.answerText">What happened</span>
            <em data-i18n="pr.whenAnswered">once answered</em>
            <textarea data-ptx="answer_text" data-col="b" rows="3"></textarea></label>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ms-grid ms-neutral">
        <label class="fld">
          <span data-i18n="pr.answeredOn">Date answered</span>
          <em data-i18n="ms.optional">optional</em>
          <input type="date" id="prAnsweredOn">
        </label>
        <label class="fld">
          <span data-i18n="ms.sortDate">Order</span>
          <em data-i18n="ms.orderingOnly">for ordering only</em>
          <input type="number" id="prSort" step="1" value="0">
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="ms-switches">
        <button type="button" class="switch" id="prPublic" role="switch" aria-checked="false">
          <span class="switch-track"><span class="switch-state">Off</span><span class="switch-knob"></span></span>
          <span class="switch-label"><span data-i18n="ms.published">Published</span>
            <span class="switch-note" data-i18n="ms.publishedNote">Visible on partner websites</span>
          </span>
        </button>
        {#- A boolean, not a status. A prayer is being asked or it has been
           answered; an enum here would invite "in progress", which is not a
           thing anybody means. -#}
        <button type="button" class="switch" id="prAnswered" role="switch" aria-checked="false">
          <span class="switch-track"><span class="switch-state">Off</span><span class="switch-knob"></span></span>
          <span class="switch-label"><span data-i18n="pr.answered">Answered</span>
            <span class="switch-note" data-i18n="pr.answeredNote">Shown with the account of what happened</span>
          </span>
        </button>
      </div>

      <div class="ms-actions">
        <button type="submit" class="solid-btn" data-i18n="pr.save">Save request</button>
        <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="prCancel" data-i18n="ms.cancel">Cancel</button>
        <span class="hint" id="prFormStatus" data-i18n="gl.savesNow">Saves immediately</span>
      </div>
    </form>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================== VIDEOS -->
{#- THE ODD ONE OUT, and worth saying why.

   The other three sections edit words somebody typed here. This one edits ONE
   field — which channel — and everything shown below it was written on
   YouTube by whoever uploaded the video. There is no editor because there is
   nothing here to edit: correcting a title means correcting it on YouTube,
   and within the quarter hour this follows.

   So no row panel, no save bar, no language columns. A field, a switch, and a
   list you can look at to confirm the right channel is attached. -#}
<section class="tab-panel" data-panel="videos" role="tabpanel" hidden>

  <div class="ms-bar">
    <span class="hint" id="vidStatus"></span>
  </div>

  <p class="note ms-note" data-i18n-html="vid.lede"><b>Videos are pulled from YouTube, not uploaded here.</b> Point this at a
    channel and the newest videos are read from its public feed every fifteen
    minutes, then served to partner websites through the same API as everything
    else on this page.</p>

  <form class="ms-form vid-form" id="vidForm">
    <label class="fld">
      <span data-i18n="vid.channel">YouTube channel</span>
      <em data-i18n="vid.channelHint">its web address, its @handle, or its id</em>
      <input type="text" id="vidChannel" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"
             placeholder="https://www.youtube.com/@yourchannel">
    </label>

    {#- Shown only once a channel has resolved, because before then there is
       nothing truthful to put in it. It is the confirmation that the thing
       the person typed found the thing they meant. -#}
    <p class="vid-found" id="vidFound" hidden></p>

    <div class="ms-grid ms-neutral">
      <label class="fld">
        <span data-i18n="vid.count">How many to show</span>
        <em data-i18n="vid.countHint">newest first</em>
        <input type="number" id="vidCount" min="1" max="15" step="1" value="3">
      </label>
    </div>

    <div class="ms-switches">
      <button type="button" class="switch" id="vidPublic" role="switch" aria-checked="false">
        <span class="switch-track"><span class="switch-state">Off</span><span class="switch-knob"></span></span>
        <span class="switch-label"><span data-i18n="ms.published">Published</span>
          <span class="switch-note" data-i18n="vid.publishedNote">Sent to partner websites, and checked every fifteen minutes</span>
        </span>
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="ms-actions">
      <button type="submit" class="solid-btn" data-i18n="vid.save">Save channel</button>
      <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="vidCheck" data-i18n="vid.check">Check now</button>
      <button type="button" class="ghost-btn danger" id="vidClear" data-i18n="vid.clear">Remove channel</button>
      <span class="hint" id="vidFormStatus" data-i18n="gl.savesNow">Saves immediately</span>
    </div>
  </form>

  {#- WHY THE SYNC REPORTS ITSELF ON SCREEN. A scheduled job has nobody to tell
     when it fails, so it writes the reason onto the channel and this is where
     that surfaces. Without it, "the videos stopped updating" is a question
     only answerable by reading Cloudflare's logs. -#}
  <p class="vid-sync" id="vidSync" hidden></p>

  <div class="vid-list" id="vidList"></div>
</section>

<div class="ms-savebar" id="msSaveBar" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden>
  <span class="ms-dirty-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span id="msDirtyCount">0 unsaved changes</span>
  <span class="ms-savebar-note" data-i18n="ms.notLive">Nothing is live until you save.</span>
  <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="msDiscard" data-i18n="ms.discard">Discard</button>
  <button type="button" class="solid-btn" id="msSaveAll" data-i18n="ms.save">Save changes</button>
</div>
